the Solution class`,\n104:         calculationCard: null,\n105:         whatItMeans:\n106:           `Python reads \\`class Solution:\\` in **Global Scope**, which is a container that holds our method. Creating the class does not calculate the answer yet—it just prepares the container.`,\n107:         variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n108:         whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n109:         finalBanner: null\n110:       };\n111:     }\n112: \n113:     // 2. Method / Function definition\n114:     if (step.eventType === \"METHOD_DEF\" || step.eventType === \"FUNC_DEF\") {\n115:       return {\n116:         title: `Step ${n}: Define the ${op.funcName} function`,\n117:         calculationCard: null,\n118:         whatItMeans:\n119:           `Python registers the function \\`${op.funcName}(${(op.params || [\"nums\"]).join(\", \")})\\` in **Global Scope**. Python only creates a **Local Scope** for this function when we call it.`,\n120:         variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n121:         whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n122:         finalBanner: null\n123:       };\n124:     }\n125: \n126:     // 3. Function Call\n127:     if (step.eventType === \"FUNC_CALL\") {\n128:       const bindings = op.paramBindings || [];\n129:       const bText = bindings.map((b) => `\\`${b.param}\\` → \\`${b.val}\\``).join(\", \");\n130:       return {\n131:         title: `Step ${n}: Call ${op.funcName}() & create Local Scope`,\n132:         calculationCard: null,\n133:         whatItMeans: bindings.length\n134:           ? `We call \\`${op.funcName}()\\` and open a new **Local Scope** stack frame! Parameter names (${bText}) now point directly to the argument addresses on the **Heap**.`\n135:           : `We call \\`${op.funcName}()\\` and enter a new **Local Scope** to execute its lines.`,\n136:         variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n137:         whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n138:         finalBanner: null\n139:       };\n140:     }\n141: \n142:     // 4. Standard variable assignment\n143:     if (step.eventType === \"ASSIGN\") {\n144:       const changedAddr = (step.variables || []).find((v) => v.name === op.target)?.address;\n145:       const addrNote = changedAddr ? ` (pointing to heap address \\`${changedAddr}\\`)` : \"\";\n146: \n147:       if (op.target === \"c\" && op.isCreated) {\n148:         return {\n149:           title: `Step ${n}: Create the variable c`,\n150:           calculationCard: null,\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
